THE FULL REQUEST PATH (MEMORISE THIS)
-------------------------------------
 browser
   -> DNS: shop.local -> load balancer / node IP
   -> LB / NodePort / hostPort
   -> ingress controller pod (matches host + path)
   -> Service "frontend" (ClusterIP, kube-proxy DNAT)
   -> frontend pod
        -> calls http://backend (CoreDNS -> ClusterIP)
        -> Service "backend" (kube-proxy DNAT)
        -> backend pod


NETWORK TROUBLESHOOTING ORDER
-----------------------------
1. Pods Running and READY?          k get pods -o wide
2. Service selects them?            k get endpointslices ... (not empty?)
3. Port numbers right?              port / targetPort / containerPort
4. DNS resolves?                    nslookup from a debug pod
5. Works by ClusterIP but not name? -> DNS. By pod IP but not
                                       ClusterIP? -> kube-proxy/Service.
6. Ingress rules + class correct?   k describe ingress; controller logs
7. NetworkPolicy blocking? (Week 5)
